# /new-page — New Page Workflow

Full workflow for a new page on the Factorial webpage (`webpage/`).
You drive. The user can skip any step.

---

## Present the Step Plan

```
/new-page workflow

  [1] Brief confirmation (URL, purpose, sections, locales)
  [2] Route setup (route group, layout, page.tsx)
  [3] Sections planning (which CMS sections, which need building)
  [4] SEO & i18n (metadata, locale routing, sitemap)
  [5] Design polish review
  [6] QA (3 breakpoints × 2 locales)
  [7] Combined report

Type a step number to skip, or press Enter to start with step 1.
```

---

## Step 1 — Brief Confirmation

Ask in a single block:

1. **URL / slug** — what will the path be? (e.g. `/integrations/xero`, `/solutions/retail`)
2. **Purpose** — what does this page do? (SEO landing, campaign, feature showcase, etc.)
3. **Locales** — which TLDs need this page? (en-US, es-ES, de-DE, fr-FR…)
4. **Sections** — what content sections does it need? (hero, feature grid, testimonials, CTA, etc.)
5. **Route group** — is it a standard marketing page `(full-layout)`, a demo flow `(demo)`, or a split-intention page `(split-intention)`?
6. **ISR** — any special revalidation requirement, or use default 1800s?

Produce a one-paragraph summary and confirm.

---

## Step 2 — Route Setup

Follow the `/webpage-page` patterns:

**File:** `webpage/app/[locale]/(route-group)/[slug]/page.tsx`

```tsx
// Always async server component — NEVER 'use client'
import type { AppPageProps } from '@/app/[locale]/types/pageProps'

export default async function Page(props: AppPageProps) {
  const { locale } = await props.params
  const tld = findTldByLocale(locale)
  if (!tld) notFound()

  // ... fetch DatoCMS data ...

  return <PageContent ... />
}

export const revalidate = 1800  // default — override only if needed
```

**Checklist:**
- [ ] `await props.params` and `await props.searchParams` (Next.js 15 Promises)
- [ ] `findTldByLocale(locale)` + `notFound()` guard for unsupported locales
- [ ] `generateMetadata` export with title, description, canonical URL
- [ ] `generateStaticParams` if page has dynamic segments
- [ ] `commonPageProps(locale)` passed to client components that need it
- [ ] Page added to sitemap (check `webpage/app/sitemap.ts` or equivalent)

---

## Step 3 — Sections Planning

List all sections the page needs. For each:

| Section | Exists? | Action |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Hero | ✅ `HeroA` | Use existing |
| Feature grid | ✅ `FeatureGrid` | Use existing |
| Testimonials | ❌ | Run `/new-section` |
| CTA banner | ✅ `CtaBanner` | Use existing |

For sections that need building, offer to run `/new-section` inline for each one
before proceeding to QA.

---

## Step 4 — SEO & i18n

**Metadata:**
```tsx
export async function generateMetadata(props: AppPageProps): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { locale } = await props.params
  return {
    title: '[Page Title] | Factorial',
    description: '[150 char description]',
    alternates: {
      canonical: `https://factorialhr.com/[slug]`,
      languages: { /* hreflang entries for each TLD */ }
    }
  }
}
```

**i18n checklist:**
- [ ] All copy goes through `intl.formatMessage()` — no raw strings in JSX
- [ ] Server-side: `getImperativeIntl(tld)` for data fetching layer
- [ ] Spanish copy tested — ~20% longer, check all text containers
- [ ] If copy is bulk/campaign (not going through Crowdin): use dictionary pattern

**Locale routing:**
- [ ] Page only renders for supported TLDs — `notFound()` guard in place
- [ ] URL structure consistent with existing page conventions

---

## Step 5 — Design Polish Review

Apply the `/design-engineer` lens. Check:

**Above-the-fold (first paint):**
- Is the key message immediately clear without scrolling?
- Hero enters with appropriate animation (word stagger, or fade — not both)
- CLS: images have explicit width/height or use `fill` with sized container

**Scroll flow:**
- Natural reading order — does the page tell a story top to bottom?
- No more than 3 animated sections — animation should guide, not overwhelm
- Consistent section spacing (check rhythm, not just individual sections)

**CTAs:**
- Primary CTA uses `radical` color tokens
- Never more than 2 CTAs visible at once
- Sticky CTA (if present) doesn't obscure content on mobile

**Output:**

| Before | After | Why |
|--------|-------|-----|
| ... | ... | ... |

---

## Step 6 — QA

Test matrix:

| | 375px | 768px | 1440px |
|---|---|---|---|
| **en-US** | ☐ | ☐ | ☐ |
| **es-ES** | ☐ | ☐ | ☐ |

Additional checks:
- [ ] Page loads without JS errors
- [ ] `<title>` and meta description correct in page source
- [ ] Canonical URL correct
- [ ] All images load with correct alt text
- [ ] All CTA links point to correct destinations
- [ ] No layout shift on image load (check with throttled network)
- [ ] Dark/reduced-motion variants look correct

URLs:
`https://webpage-{tld}.local.factorial.dev/[slug]`
(Replace `{tld}` with `us`, `es`, `de` etc.)

